From 2d21f1b33c9fa896e25ee1adf759cb4e74be5892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:50:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prose profile: the volume is called Prose

The disk Tracker shows on the desktop, and its window title, said "Haiku":
HAIKU_IMAGE_LABEL and HAIKU_MMC_LABEL both default to that name. The
prose-* profile sets them, as it already sets the host name.

Nothing reads the label -- the boot loader finds the partition by its
contents and /boot is the mount point either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0049-prose-profile-the-volume-is-called-prose.patch a784d31f8b5e85c690b15f27885602d40dc3982e207723a70c4c77ea785515a5
---
 build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
index b20ce36e5b..f2a5e5d2cc 100644
--- a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
+++ b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
@@ -194,6 +194,9 @@ rule DefineDefaultBuildProfiles
 		case "prose-*" : {
 			Echo Building Prose ;
 			HAIKU_IMAGE_HOST_NAME ?= prose ;
+			# the volume Tracker shows on the desktop, and the boot partition
+			HAIKU_IMAGE_LABEL ?= Prose ;
+			HAIKU_MMC_LABEL ?= Prose ;
 			if $(DEBUG) != 0 {
 				HAIKU_IMAGE_SIZE ?= 850 ;
 			}
